  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "No chapter describes its appearance.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu tribe’s leader says the tribe has received a lot of help from them. Wu Shuai treats the news as good. Humanity dominates, Gu tribe hides at the bottom of the sea, and a close relationship with mermen is unsurprising. The court had once received support from Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        1862
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_tribe",
        "char_wu_shuai",
        "race_humans",
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eastern Sea’s Merman Imperial Court is a super force with deep foundations, the sole variant human super force in the world, able to develop and continue because it received Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable’s help. Its higher-ups have been helping Gu tribe in secret, and the court has begun investing everywhere for the survival of their tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        1868
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "deep-foundations",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tang Qiong, a yellow scaled mermaid, greets Wu Shuai as an elder in charge of the Merman Imperial Court and as its representative. She says her Imperial Court received Qi Sea Ancestor’s banquet invitation and that the grand elder wants to know if Wu Shuai will go with them. Wu Shuai notes that he has rank eight Immortal Gu House Dragon Palace while the Merman Imperial Court has no rank eight Immortal Gu House, and that their force was established with Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable’s help.",
      "chapters": [
        1879
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "elder-representative",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tang_qiong",
        "loc_imperial_court",
        "char_qi_sea_ancestor",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_dragon_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Eastern Sea, Merman Imperial Court. At a grand banquet, three female immortals leading the court sit on the main seats: Lian Ke Xin, Yu Zi, and Xie Ning Si. They entertain Ice Crystal Immortal Monarch. Yu Zi answers that they have more than ten Gu Immortals and Immortal Gu House Floating Reputation Boat. In a three-round bet, the court uses Floating Reputation Boat in the second round and loses after a hundred rounds of fighting.",
      "chapters": [
        1979
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "banquet-contest",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "char_lian_ke_xin",
        "char_yu_zi",
        "char_ice_crystal_immortal_monarch",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_floating_reputation_boat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xia clan sits at the easternmost area of Eastern Sea. Toward their west is the Merman Imperial Court, toward the southeast is Tang clan, and toward the northeast is Xie clan. Those three border Xia clan in territory. Xia clan’s relationship with the Merman Imperial Court is the best of the three, but they are variant humans, and Xia clan’s immortals carefully go past the court toward Shen clan, further west, for help.",
      "chapters": [
        1985
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "territorial-neighbors",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_xia_clan",
        "fac_tang_clan",
        "fac_xie_clan",
        "fac_shen_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Southern Border’s Mushroomman Paradise, Eastern Sea’s Merman Imperial Court, and the blue dragon whale had all received Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable’s help.",
      "chapters": [
        2059
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-with-others",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "loc_mushroomman_paradise"
      ]
    }
  ],
